  "query_preview": "..\nA persistent trough hangs over California, continuing our\nsouthwesterly breezes this afternoon and less so tomorrow.\nGenerally, it has been observed 25 to 30 mph across Southeast \nArizona with a peak gust of 36 mph at Pioneer Airfield. This \nwill continue through the rest of the day. Dry conditions as\nwell, bringing elevated fire weather concerns. \n\nGoing forward, the California trough will retrograde with a\nridge of high pressure building over the intermountain west.\nThere will be some breezes tomorrow, but less than today. As the\nridge builds, temperatures will trend warmer this weekend. Moderate\nHeatRisk will return for the region wide by Sunday and into the\nnew week.\n\nUpper level flow will shift towards the weekend, opening up to \nsoutherly flow and the return of monsoon moisture. Precipitable\nwater content will push into the region by Friday, mainly in \nthe form of clouds. Values will continue to rise up to the 75th\npercentile by Monday, therefore introducing chances for showers\nand thunderstorms. Daily chances will expand and continue \nthrough the new week as the high pressure ebbs and bobs around \nthe desert southwest. Models are consistent of high pressure \nstaying, but variation on the center's location; influencing the\nflow of moisture and the best areas for precipitation.",
